```

This test verifies that `ArrayList.LastIndexOf` operation produces correct index in given ArrayList. The test takes an assumed ArrayList and an int as parameters. The assumptions include that ArrayList contains integer number and the integer is present in ArrayList. In the postcondition, the test verifies that the new return value is more than the old index of integer in the ArrayList to show that it correctly locates the last index of the integer in the ArrayList.

## Generating the Test

When you run the test in Microsoft Visual Studio 2015 and later, the test generates code coverage. 

Open the generated test in another Visual Studio window. The code for the PexGeneric.Test.PUT_LastIndexOfContract test case is given below. 

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[HostType("Moles")]
[DataRow(new object[] { new ArrayList() {new int[] {1, 2, 4, 3, 1, 4, 5 }} } , new object[] { 1 } )]
public void PUT_LastIndexOfContract(ArrayList arrList, int x)
{
    // Arrange
    int Old_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
    int Old_x = x;
    int Old_arrListIndexOfX = arrList.IndexOf(x);
    bool Old_arrListContainsX = arrList.Contains(x);

    // Act
    int New_Ret = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);

    // Assert
    Assert.IsTrue(New_Ret > Old_arrListIndexOfX);
}
```
This test code checks that the LastIndexOf function returns an index greater than the IndexOf function of the old list.

## Testing the Code 

To Test the ArrayList Contract, launch the Microsoft Visual Studio 2015 Ultimate with the Pex Feature installed. Open up the project containing the ArrayList class. After that, click on Test >> New >> Test with Code Generation. In the Test Wizard that opens, select the ArrayList option and then click Next. Under ArrayList Contracts, select LastIndexOf and then click Finish.

The generated test is run and can be seen in the Test Results. It verifies that LastIndexOf returns a higher value that IndexOf when called on an ArrayList. 

## Running Pex with PBT 
You can use Pex with PBT (Property-Based Testing) to ensure your code meets a wide range of user inputs. In addition to LastIndexOf, Pex also checks Clear, Contains, CopyTo, IndexOf, Insert, Remove, and Sort methods of ArrayList. 

By using Pex with PBT, you can quickly verify your code correctness with a large number of test cases generated automatically.






































































